Description: Client-side DataSHIELD functions for privacy-aware analysis
    of vertically partitioned federated data. The audited active surface covers
    record alignment, reusable differential-privacy capsules, bounded
    descriptives, categorical tables, epidemiological post-processing,
    correlation, PCA and selected Gaussian and penalised research workflows
    over the companion dsVert server package. Public names for Cox PH and
    selected negative-binomial, multinomial and ordinal intercept-only
    post-processors remain available over validated sticky artifacts. The
    LMM, GLMM, IPW and categorical multiple-imputation compatibility names
    likewise expose only their documented signed-artifact scopes; covariate,
    REML/PQL, clustered-inference, weighting and chained-imputation variants
    fail locally before DSI. An audited
    maturity registry distinguishes conditional promoted methods, provisional
    research routes, historical compatibility helpers and quarantined
    estimators. Peer pinning and MPC protect protocol intermediates.
    Dedicated ds.vertDP* releases use a persistent, memoizing, cross-signed
    publication ledger with server-owned contribution bounds. Composition
    history is informational and never an operation or request quota; legacy
    exact outputs remain outside that DP guarantee and do not support a
    non-reconstruction claim under unlimited adaptive queries.
